Ugathal, in their inert form, are pink, fleshy creatures made of ropes of muscle and sinew twisted into a vaguely humanoid shape. They can steal the bodies of their victims, extracting the flesh off a corpse and wearing it as disguise.

An Ugathal inside a stolen body passes for a person until it chooses to stop. Then it swells by a foot and a half, its clothing sinks into its flesh, its eyes withdraw into their sockets, and the rest of the face smooths over into a blank, mouthless mask. They hunt in pairs, and they laugh with a wet gargling sound.

Cut one open and there is no blood inside, only more flesh. They give no sign of feeling a wound even as their bodies come apart; a blade opens them, while a hammer blow hardly marks them. What they catch, they hold, and a held victim is pinned in place while a proboscis grows from the blank face to drink their blood. The pair that ambushed a group in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] had [[Blackline]] badges lodged inside their flesh.
